# Security & Privacy

## Purpose

Lens captures real request/response/query/mail data. This rule keeps secrets and PII out of the
store and the dashboard.

## Why it exists

A debugging tool that records credentials, tokens, or personal data becomes a liability and a
breach vector. Redaction and purging are core features, not optional add-ons.

## Redaction is centralized in the RequestWatcher

`RequestWatcher.log(data, hidden)`
([request_watcher.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/watchers/request_watcher.ts)) is the single place
request headers/body are hidden. It lowercases header keys and replaces matched keys with
`"*******"`. Defaults:

- Headers: `Authorization`, `Basic`.
- Body params: `password`, `passwordConfirmation`, `secret`, `password_confirmation`.

Consumers extend these via `config.hiddenParams.{headers,bodyParams}`
([LensConfig](mdc:packages/core/src/types/index.ts)). Adapters MUST forward `config.hiddenParams`
as the second argument to `requestWatcher.log(...)`. Never build request logging that bypasses
this hiding.

## Purge large / binary / file bodies

Adapters replace file-path, `Buffer`, and non-serializable response bodies with the literal
`"Purged By Lens"` (express `patchResponseMethods`, fastify `parseResponsePayload`). Preserve
this — never store raw file contents or buffers.

## Gate user data behind auth callbacks

Attach `user` only when `await config.isAuthenticated?.(req)` is true, then
`await config.getUser?.(req)`; otherwise `user: null`. Never infer/scrape user identity from
raw headers or bodies.

## General rules

- Never `console.log` captured payloads; log only operational events (connect, queue overflow,
  save error).
- Never add real secrets/tokens/PII to tests, fixtures, sample `.eml` files, changesets, or
  docs examples. Use obviously fake values.
- Treat the dashboard + Lens API as sensitive: they expose captured data. Do not add endpoints
  that return more than the existing `ApiController` surface, and keep Lens's own routes in the
  `prepareIgnoredPaths` ignore list so Lens does not record itself.
- When adding a new watcher/handler, redact or omit sensitive fields BEFORE `save()`/`emit()`
  (mirror the RequestWatcher approach); assume every captured field may contain secrets.

## AI must never

- Persist or log secrets, tokens, credentials, or PII.
- Add request/response capture that skips `hiddenParams` redaction or body purging.
- Weaken the default hidden headers/body params, or store raw files/buffers.
- Commit real credentials in code, tests, fixtures, or documentation.
